{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791429402,"nonce":"cUtJq+OVfvUx4pfiAeQZvAvrFHc=","message":"Held after validation. Removing all outgoing native probes when Cranelift is the final tier is semantically valid and speeds many kernels, but LU regresses from about 670 to 775 ms wall (478 to 585 ms kernel) on the NUC. Same-binary force-probes control restores it. Changing minimum function alignment to 16/32/64 bytes did not resolve the regression. Forwarding HIR cold-call annotations to Cranelift marks 56 LU blocks cold but also does not resolve it. Cross-block load reuse reduces the slowdown but adds startup costs elsewhere.\n\nThe default probe behavior is restored for the accepted counter-vectorization candidate. The gate patch is preserved in /tmp/zyntax-final-tier-and-policy.patch and /tmp/zyntax-tiered-with-probe-gate.rs locally. Do not close this issue or advertise the roughly 33 ms call-loop wall time as landed: that result depends on the held probe gate. Safe SIMD with existing probes is roughly 47 ms versus 74 ms before; final validation pending. Interpreter-first dispatch and incoming interpreter-to-Cranelift OSR are retained in either candidate.","files":null}]}